# FY26 Emissions Data
# Emissions accounting for Scope 3 reduction planning (tCO2e). data_quality: measured = from supplier or meter data, estimated = modelled or spend-based

scope,category,tonnes_co2e,data_quality,source_allocation
Scope1,Direct,5273,measured,Owned facilities and vehicles
Scope2,Indirect Power,12236,measured,Purchased electricity
Scope3,Purchased goods and materials,55402,estimated,Suppliers and materials (spend-based)
Scope3,Transportation,17309,estimated,Inbound and outbound freight
Scope3,Use of Products,11067,estimated,Customer use phase and end of life
Scope3,Other,2358,mixed,Employee commuting and business travel

SUMMARY:
Total emissions: 103,644 tCO2e. Scope 3 total: 86,135 tCO2e (83% of the total).

LEVER INPUTS:
Air freight: about 4,900 tCO2e a year from 985 tonnes of goods flown (measured volumes, emissions estimated). Sea freight alternative carries the same goods at about 130 tCO2e with a 4-week longer lead time.
Shifting 30% of air freight to sea: about 1,440 tCO2e a year saved (estimate, net of sea emissions).
Recycled polyester across basics: about 950 tCO2e a year at full conversion (estimate, about 250 tonnes of polyester fibre at 2.6 instead of 6.4 kg CO2e per kg, supplier-average factors, not verified).
Top 20 suppliers: 45,840 tCO2e (53.2% of Scope 3, 84% of it estimated). About 13% of that, 6,000 tCO2e, is purchased electricity that renewable electricity would remove (estimate).
